        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCU footprints are populated, two microcontrollers drive the same lines, causing contention and unpredictable behavior. If U1 is used, it cannot be programmed through the existing AVR-ISP header because the header is wired for ATtiny13 MISO/SCK on PB1/PB2 rather than ATtiny45 MISO/SCK on PB3/PB4.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show two ATtiny MCUs connected in parallel, with ISP signals matching only the ATtiny13 pinout, which deviates from the intended single ATtiny fan controller and can cause contention or unprogrammability."
}

